        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"448405\">Alex Meiburg</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/New.20member.20PR.20.2337705/near/583861341\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>You should really try to clean up the proofs somewhat. I looked at <code>mgf_sq_gaussianReal</code> as a case. For one thing, there's a lint message you should have seen: <code>ring</code> highlights and tells you to change it to <code>ring_nf</code>. The <code>have ht'</code> is never used in the proof and can be deleted without issue. The <code>simp_rw [show ∀ x : ℝ, ... from fun x =&gt; by rw [...]; ...]</code> is way too nested. The <code>[hsqrt2pi_pos.ne']</code> argument to <code>field_simp</code> is also unneeded. <code>have ht12 : 0 &lt; 1 - 2 * t</code> is only used in one place, where it's <code>le_of_lt ht12</code>, so why not make it <code>have ht12 : 0 ≤ 1 - 2 * t</code>? The <code>congr 1</code> is unnecessary since it's just <code>ring_nf</code> after. And so on.</p>\n<p>Here's a first-pass \"local cleanup\", although actually looking at the algebraic manipulations for the last ~10 lines I'm sure there's a shorter golf:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ProbabilityTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mgf_sq_gaussianReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ht</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">mgf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">gaussianReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- mgf (·^2) γ t = ∫ x, exp(t·x²) ∂γ = ∫ x, pdfReal(x)·exp(t·x²) dx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">mgf</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">integral_gaussianReal_eq_integral_smul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">one_ne_zero</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">gaussianPDFReal</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NNReal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coe_one</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_one</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sub_zero</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">smul_eq_mul</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Combine the two exponentials under the integral</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_comb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">√</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">√</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">⁻¹</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">mul_assoc</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exp_add</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ring_nf</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp_rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h_comb</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MeasureTheory</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">integral_const_mul</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">integral_gaussian</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">suffices</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">√</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">√</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">field_simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_simpl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">√</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">sq_sqrt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">positivity</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">field_simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h_simpl</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sqrt_div'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sqrt_sq</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sqrt_eq_rpow</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sqrt_eq_rpow</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">div_eq_mul_inv</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rpow_neg</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linarith</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">positivity</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linarith</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>You should try to do this for all of the lemmas! Also, many of the comments don't make any sense.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Thank you Alex for the extremely valuable and thoughtful feedback.  I have no calibration on how to productively contribute to Lean but feel compelled to as it is such an extremely important community and technology.  Full disclosure,  I am not a mathematician but I am (hopefully) exploring and extremely ambitious project that if successful may be able to facilitate those of you that are.  Re-working  PR as we speak and of course learning.   Best!</p>",
        "id": 583877998,
        "sender_full_name": "Ted Vucurevich",
        "timestamp": 1775513839
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><strong>@Alex Meiburg</strong> — thank you again for the thorough code review. All six items have been addressed:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>ring</code> → <code>ring_nf</code> ✓</li>\n<li>Removed unused <code>ht'</code>, <code>ht12</code>, and the <code>hsqrt2pi_pos.ne'</code> argument to <code>field_simp</code> ✓</li>\n<li>Replaced the nested <code>simp_rw [show ∀ x ...]</code> with a named <code>h_comb</code> lemma ✓</li>\n<li>Applied the same cleanup across <code>Inequalities.lean</code> (<code>simpa</code> pattern, named <code>hdeq</code>) ✓</li>\n<li>Removed all inline step-narration comments ✓</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These changes are currently in a staging repo (<a href=\"https://github.com/Wolfman56/lean-publish\">https://github.com/Wolfman56/lean-publish</a>) while I review and run a broader feedback solicitation pass before pushing to the PR branch. A few open questions are documented in [PR_REVIEW_BATON.md] — notably around the squared vs distance form of the JL conclusion, the <code>log(n(n-1))</code> hypothesis form, and whether <code>smul_mulVec_real</code> already exists in Mathlib. I'll push the updated branch once that review is complete and happy to address any further feedback then.</p>",
        "id": 583908439,
        "sender_full_name": "Ted Vucurevich",
        "timestamp": 1775534646
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, my point wasn't that these were things specifically with that lemma, but rather that <em>all the code</em> should be written to a cleaner standard. This is something that it hard to get done if you don't write much Lean yourself, so if you want to get code merged into Mathlib, I encourage you to go and practice writing proofs yourself so you can learn about how to condense and clean. Mathlib does have AI-written code, but it's typically from people very experienced with Lean to begin with.</p>\n<p>As a side note, your last message looks very LLM written. While AI generated code is an artifact to be checked in some where, in terms of personal communication, I (and many others) find it rude to be \"talking to an LLM\" through someone else.</p>",
        "id": 584018392,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1775574395
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hi <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"448405\">@Alex Meiburg</span> ,   Again  Thanks for the feedback, I've always been a learn by doing kind of guy so appreciate the precise feedback.   Only the bullets were copied from my interactive session with multiple agents and specialized contexts as we precisely reviewed them.  Everything else is me for better or worse.  Honestly, not sure if I have the time or the capacity to do pure human only contribution at this point.  To be honest,  this was a missing proof from MathLib,  which I am using in the much broader context of Human + AI collaboration based on sound mathematical models.  This PR was humbly contributed as a \"gap\" filler.  Nothing more.  I noticed <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"634338\">@Michael Rothgang</span> Robot?  Must be the chat convention (again, not familiar with the protocols) for \"not written by human\".      I'll definitely continue to update my lean-publish repo as reproducible results from my personal work and who knows,  that work may help lower the interdisciplinary barrier for future contribution.   Best, Ted</p>",
        "id": 584027181,
        "sender_full_name": "Ted Vucurevich",
        "timestamp": 1775576586
    }
]